        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "refactor(config): retire flat streaming keys from the last six channel schemas via doctor migration",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nAfter #104693/#105054, six bundled channels still treated flat streaming keys as canonical config: signal and irc (core schemas), nextcloud-talk and irc again (via the shared `ReplyRuntimeConfigSchemaShape`), whatsapp, googlechat, and mattermost (which additionally accepted scalar/boolean `streaming` as a mode). That split kept the SDK resolvers' flat fallback load-bearing for bundled channels and left users with two config dialects. None of the migrated-channel work has shipped in a release tag yet, so completing the retirement now gives users a single migration event in one release train.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\n- All six channels move to nested `streaming.{chunkMode,block.enabled,block.coalesce}` (mattermost also `streaming.mode`, retiring its scalar/boolean form). Schemas reject flat keys; `openclaw doctor --fix` migrates via `defineChannelAliasMigration` specs (#105636), with per-channel semantics determined from runtime source: signal/irc/nextcloud-talk/whatsapp/googlechat are `deliveryOnly` (no preview mode); mattermost resolves `partial` for both absent and object-without-mode so no default pinning is needed.\n- Account seeding follows each channel's real merge semantics. Five channels use the DSL's `accountStreamingReplacesRoot`; WhatsApp has an extra `accounts.default` shared layer between root and named accounts, so it gets plugin-local layered seeding (including case-insensitive `accounts.Default`, matching `resolveAccountEntry`) — an autoreview-caught correctness fix that the generic DSL path could not express without core learning WhatsApp's layering.\n- Bespoke flat reads deleted: signal monitor, irc/nextcloud-talk inbound gates, whatsapp account-config/monitor/inbound-dispatch — all now resolve through the shared SDK resolvers.\n- The SDK resolvers' flat fallback now warns once per process per key (`Flat channel streaming key \"…\" is deprecated; move it to streaming.…; removed after the next release train.`), making remaining consumers visible instead of guessed. Warn-once state lives outside `streaming.ts` so the `export *` SDK barrels don't leak test-reset hooks.\n- Docs updated (`docs/concepts/streaming.md`, `messages.md`, signal/nextcloud-talk/whatsapp/mattermost channel pages, `docs/gateway/config-channels.md` including a stale telegram scalar example); bundled channel config metadata and the plugin-sdk API baseline regenerated.\n\n## User Impact\n\n- One canonical streaming config shape across these six channels; existing flat-key configs are blocked loudly at startup and rewritten behavior-preservingly by `openclaw doctor --fix` (inheritance-aware for multi-account setups).\n- Third-party SDK plugins keep working through the flat fallback for one more train, now with an explicit deprecation warning and removal date.\n- Known residual (documented in-code and in docs): matrix and feishu plugin schemas (and qqbot's scalar `streaming`) still accept flat/scalar forms — follow-up PR before the fallback-removal train.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Per-channel semantics determinations with file:line evidence in the review artifacts (e.g. whatsapp layering `extensions/whatsapp/src/account-config.ts:41-67`; mattermost `resolveChannelPreviewStreamMode(merged, \"partial\")` at `extensions/mattermost/src/mattermost/accounts.ts:138`; shared-shape consumers enumerated: irc + nextcloud-talk only).\n- Blacksmith Testbox: target suites green except 12 pre-existing failures in two whatsapp test files (`WhatsApp runtime not initialized`) — proven unrelated: identical failures at the branch base and on clean `origin/main` (leases `tbx_01kxc0snzm4vd0vzjaar0c5495`, `tbx_01kxc102h3rbmea166sc8730tn`; post-rebase re-run `tbx_01kxc2gmct85rd30k7qgk7smv5`); tracked as a separate task chip. Full remote `check:changed` green (lease `tbx_01kxc1g9khdseb7vg9egj6m64s`, 11m43s; post-rebase re-run green).\n- Autoreview (codex gpt-5.6-sol xhigh), six rounds per-commit: three accepted findings fixed (whatsapp `accounts.default` layer lost in seeding; docs overgeneralizing \"all bundled channels\"; case-insensitive default-account key), final round clean (0.97).\n- Fires-once deprecation warning covered by tests (once per key, all four keys, silent when nested config present).\n\nRefs #104693, #105054, #105636. Follow-up: matrix/feishu/qqbot flat retirement before the fallback-removal train.\n",
        "branch": "claude/chanref-flatkeys-batch",
